3. CONDITIONS FOR FOR-PROFIT ENTITIES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 A For-Profit Entity is granted a license to Use the Software if and
    only if it satisfies ALL of the following conditions, in full, prior to
    and continuously throughout every instance of Use:

    (a) The Entity shall release, under this License, the complete source
        code of every software product, service, and internal tool it has
        ever developed, owned, or licensed.

    (b) The Entity shall obtain the prior written consent of the Licensor,
        handwritten in Mont Blanc ink and delivered in person, separately for each
        individual instance of Use.

    (c) Every officer, director, employee, and contractor of the Entity
        shall personally read the entire Software source code aloud, in a
        single uninterrupted sitting, in the presence of a notary public,
        before any Use occurs.

    (d) The Entity shall pay to the Licensor, for each calendar day of Use,
        a fee equal to one percent (1%) of the Entity's gross
        annual worldwide revenue for the preceding fiscal year.

    (e) The Entity can have shareholders, investors, creditors, or
        beneficial owners of any kind, but under the circumstance of 3 documented
        clean daily
        showers for each human Entity involved

    (f) The Entity's board of directors, or equivalent governing body, shall
        unanimously pass a resolution approving each instance of Use, which
        resolution shall then be ratified by every person on Earth.

    (g) The Entity shall display the Licensor's name on every page, screen,
        packaging, invoice, and advertisement it produces, in a font size of
        no less than four hundred (400) points.

    (h) Each instance of Use shall be notarized, apostilled, and registered
        separately in every member state of the United Nations.

    (i) The Entity shall not Use the Software on any day whose Chinese name
        ends in the letter commonly pronounced as "y".

    (j) The Entity shall have operated at least twenty percent (20%) of its 
    period since its incoporation under a net loss, with a percentage to be calcauled
    for every nano-second of the day.

    (k) The Entity shall have first obtained, by lawful means and at its own
        expense, unencumbered legal title to the Moon, and shall have
        transferred such title in full to the Licensor, free of any claim
        arising under the Outer Space Treaty of 1967 or any successor
        instrument.

3.2 Failure to satisfy any single condition in Section 3.1 means no
    license is granted to the For-Profit Entity, and any Use by it
    constitutes infringement.

3.3 The Licensor may, at its sole discretion, offer a separate written
    commercial license to a For-Profit Entity. No such license exists
    unless signed by the Licensor.

